1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,938
Pesadilla Verde: a suffocating South American jungle, a one-way river, and a squad

2
00:00:04,938 --> 00:00:07,596
of soldiers who'd rather fight than be rescued.

3
00:00:07,816 --> 00:00:09,565
Here's how the location plays.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,183
Put the Huey token in the Clearing, and the two Train cards into your Action

5
00:00:14,183 --> 00:00:14,581
Tableau.

6
00:00:14,801 --> 00:00:18,526
Lay out the Soldiers card and Action cubes, then the eight Upgrade tokens:

7
00:00:18,526 --> 00:00:21,244
the two green starters unlocked, the other six locked.

8
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:26,389
Every normal Victim here is a Soldier, sent into the conflict zone and eager to

9
00:00:26,389 --> 00:00:26,717
fight.

10
00:00:26,937 --> 00:00:29,858
For almost every game effect they count as normal Victims:

11
00:00:29,858 --> 00:00:32,527
they follow you, panic, get killed, and can be saved.

12
00:00:32,747 --> 00:00:36,632
But there are two big differences. Soldiers WILL follow you into the Killer's space.

13
00:00:36,632 --> 00:00:37,973
And you can give them orders.

14
00:00:38,193 --> 00:00:42,369
The two Special Victims, the Archeologist and the Rebel Leader, are not Soldiers, so

15
00:00:42,369 --> 00:00:43,463
they can't be ordered.

16
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:48,277
What your Soldiers can do is set by eight Upgrade tokens on the Soldiers card.

17
00:00:48,497 --> 00:00:51,012
Action Upgrades are the tokens with squares on them.

18
00:00:51,012 --> 00:00:55,025
There are two Move and two Attack. You start with one Move and one Attack unlocked.

19
00:00:55,245 --> 00:00:58,002
Ability Upgrades are the four tokens without squares.

20
00:00:58,002 --> 00:01:01,539
They all start locked, and each one changes how the Soldiers behave.

21
00:01:01,759 --> 00:01:04,476
To unlock an Upgrade, flip it from its padlock side.

22
00:01:04,476 --> 00:01:06,409
If an effect locks one, flip it back.

23
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:09,409
You order Soldiers during the Action phase.

24
00:01:09,629 --> 00:01:11,975
Choose a space with one or more Soldiers in it.

25
00:01:11,975 --> 00:01:16,117
Then choose an unlocked Action Upgrade with no cube anywhere in its row, and put an

26
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:17,864
Action cube on its leftmost square.

27
00:01:18,084 --> 00:01:21,179
Every Soldier in that space carries out the action together.

28
00:01:21,179 --> 00:01:25,253
Move moves the whole group one space. Attack has them attack Enemies in a space

29
00:01:25,253 --> 00:01:26,233
within their range.

30
00:01:26,453 --> 00:01:30,467
You can give several orders in one turn, as long as each uses a different free

31
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:30,827
Action.

32
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:36,171
Actions need to recover. In each Upkeep phase, slide every Action cube one square to

33
00:01:36,171 --> 00:01:36,711
the right.

34
00:01:36,931 --> 00:01:39,528
When a cube slides off the last square, take it off:

35
00:01:39,528 --> 00:01:41,027
that Action can be used again.

36
00:01:41,247 --> 00:01:44,777
So an order you give now is unavailable for the next couple of turns.

37
00:01:44,777 --> 00:01:48,564
That's why unlocking the second Move and second Attack token is so useful.

38
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,683
Untrained, Soldiers aren't much good in a fight.

39
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:56,534
An attack does damage equal to the number of Soldiers divided by two, rounded down.

40
00:01:56,534 --> 00:02:00,607
So one Soldier alone does nothing, and three together do just one damage.

41
00:02:00,827 --> 00:02:02,981
They can only attack the space they're standing in.

42
00:02:03,201 --> 00:02:06,658
And after every Attack order, roll a die for each Soldier involved.

43
00:02:06,658 --> 00:02:10,734
On a one or two, one of the Soldiers in that attack is shot by his own side and

44
00:02:10,734 --> 00:02:11,095
killed.

45
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:14,247
Each Ability Upgrade fixes one weakness.

46
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:18,759
Saving Soldiers: they're stubborn and don't want rescuing, so saving one normally

47
00:02:18,759 --> 00:02:21,037
costs two Time. Unlocked, it costs nothing.

48
00:02:21,257 --> 00:02:24,180
Friendly Fire: unlocked, you stop rolling for friendly fire.

49
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:28,091
Attack Range: unlocked, they can attack their own space or an adjacent one.

50
00:02:28,311 --> 00:02:31,253
Damage: unlocked, divide by two and round up instead.

51
00:02:31,253 --> 00:02:34,028
Now one Soldier does one damage, and three do two.

52
00:02:34,833 --> 00:02:39,039
You unlock Upgrades with the Train Action card, which you buy like any other Action

53
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:39,292
card.

54
00:02:39,512 --> 00:02:42,037
A good result unlocks an Upgrade of your choice.

55
00:02:42,037 --> 00:02:46,403
A poor result can lock one instead, so check the card's rows before you rely on it.

56
00:02:46,623 --> 00:02:50,676
Giving orders doesn't cost Time. It's limited only by which Actions are free.

57
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:55,829
The Huey helicopter starts in the Clearing, and the space with the Huey counts as an

58
00:02:55,829 --> 00:02:56,087
exit.

59
00:02:56,307 --> 00:02:59,976
When you're in the Huey's space, you can save any number of Victims there at once.

60
00:03:00,196 --> 00:03:04,237
Then the Huey leaves: remove the token, and the Clearing stops being an exit.

61
00:03:04,237 --> 00:03:08,436
Unless a card brings the Huey back, it's a one-time escape, so fill the Clearing

62
00:03:08,436 --> 00:03:08,751
first.

63
00:03:09,567 --> 00:03:13,423
There are four River spaces: the Waterfall, the Upper River, the Central River and

64
00:03:13,423 --> 00:03:15,540
the Lower River. The arrows show the current.

65
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:20,088
Moving downriver, a single space of movement can take you to any River space further

66
00:03:20,088 --> 00:03:24,365
down. For example, one Walk success can carry you from the Waterfall all the way to

67
00:03:24,365 --> 00:03:25,189
the Lower River.

68
00:03:25,409 --> 00:03:29,185
But you pass through every space in between, and you must resolve anything there.

69
00:03:29,405 --> 00:03:32,623
Soldiers get the same fast ride when you order them to move.

70
00:03:32,623 --> 00:03:35,357
Enemies don't: they only drift one space downriver.

71
00:03:35,577 --> 00:03:39,138
No one, you, Victims or Enemies, can move upriver against the arrows.

72
00:03:39,138 --> 00:03:43,317
The space upriver still counts as adjacent, though, for attacks and anything else

73
00:03:43,317 --> 00:03:44,452
that checks adjacency.

74
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:49,439
Two cards to watch for. The Piranhas! event puts the Piranhas token on a random

75
00:03:49,439 --> 00:03:53,558
River space. Everyone there gets hurt, and so does anyone who enters it later,

76
00:03:53,558 --> 00:03:56,040
including when you pass through on the current.

77
00:03:56,260 --> 00:04:00,702
And the Cursed Sacrifice Terror card drags every Victim one space towards the Cursed

78
00:04:00,702 --> 00:04:04,826
Temple, then kills any Victims there. If none die, the two Victims nearest the

79
00:04:04,826 --> 00:04:06,201
Temple are killed instead.

80
00:04:07,033 --> 00:04:10,937
A few tips. Unlock No Friendly Fire early, or your squad thins itself out.

81
00:04:11,157 --> 00:04:15,403
Keep Soldiers together: damage is half the group, so one big squad hits far harder

82
00:04:15,403 --> 00:04:16,491
than scattered pairs.

83
00:04:16,711 --> 00:04:19,271
Gather Victims in the Clearing before you use the Huey.

84
00:04:19,491 --> 00:04:23,416
And finish anything upriver first. The river's a fast lane with no way back.

